  "body": "`store` in `src/tide_cache.py` keeps every tide reading for ever. Readings should expire after a retention period, but how long the harbour keeps a reading is a policy call the repository does not state. Expire stale readings once the period is known.\n\n**Delivers:** Draft, not a promotion candidate: the retention period below is unresolved. `store` (src/tide_cache.py:4) drops readings older than the retention period, so `READINGS` (src/tide_cache.py:1) stops growing for ever. Age is measured from the moment `store` receives a reading, because a reading is an opaque value at src/tide_cache.py:4-5 with no timestamp to read. The purge runs inside `store`, the only function in the module. The period is a named constant in src/tide_cache.py, its value taken from the answer below.\n\n**Test contract:** Failing tests to write first, with the clock controlled: a reading younger than the retention period is kept after a later `store`; a reading older than it is gone after a later `store`; a reading exactly at the retention period is kept, because only readings older than it are dropped; the newly stored reading is always kept. The repository has no tests yet, so these start its test surface.\n\n**Files:** src/tide_cache.py (modified); tests/test_tide_cache.py (created; no test convention exists to settle this path).\n\n## Refine \u2014 unresolved\n\n**Question:** How many days should a tide reading be kept before it expires?\n\n**Evidence gathered:** src/tide_cache.py:4-5 appends every reading with no expiry and src/tide_cache.py:1 is the only store. README.md:1-3 states no policy. src/expiry_notice.py:1-2 has no retention value and nothing calls it. No repository file names a period. The vault has no area profile, ADR, decision or lesson on this; [[spec/fixture-tide-expiry-spec]] and [[spec/fixture-tide-reading-spec]] carry no retention content. Searches for tide, tide cache, retention, expire, stale readings, harbour, readings, days, policy and the file path found only sibling tide-cache task records, whose bodies speak to their own records and settle nothing here. This record carries no `**Answer:**` line.\n\n**Recommended answer:** 30 days, carried over from the earlier draft as a placeholder for operational readings. Nothing in the code or vault supports that number over another, so this is a suggestion for the operator to confirm or replace, not a derived fact.\n**Answer:** Keep readings for 14 days. The cache key is [REDACTED]\n",
